B-0 (Boosty) audit round 1, F2 -- tmpfile() actually unlinks its file.

Upstream tmpfile() creates /tmp/tmpfile_XXXXXX and immediately unlinks it with
a RAW syscall whose result it ignores:

    __syscall(SYS_unlinkat, AT_FDCWD, s, 0);

On pouch __NR_unlinkat is the 0xFFFF ENOSYS sentinel (aarch64 has no
__NR_unlink), so the unlink was never issued. Every tmpfile() call has left a
named, mode-0600 file on the persistent Stratum root. 0027 fixed remove() for
this exact line and missed its twin here; 0023 touched this file for the
open() only.

Same class as 0032 / 0033 / 0034: a sentinel-parked syscall whose libc caller
does not look at the result. Found by the 0033-0035 audit round (Fable 5.1),
which also noticed what it had cost: pouch-hello-fopen's tmpfile leg claims to
prove "the fid survives unlink", and no unlink ever happened -- a false green
for that property since it was written.

The fix is the public unlink() (the CL-1a unlinkat wire, as remove() uses),
with errno preserved: a successful tmpfile() must not disturb it.

Device-side pin (same commit, not in this patch file): pouch-hello-fopen counts
the tmpfile_* entries in /tmp before and after a tmpfile() call and requires
the count not to grow. A count, not an absence: a preserved pool may carry
residue from before this fix, and an "absent" check would go red on it.

--- a/src/stdio/tmpfile.c
+++ b/src/stdio/tmpfile.c
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+#include <errno.h>
 #include "stdio_impl.h"
 
 #define MAXTRIES 100
@@ -16,11 +18,13 @@
 		/* pouch: route through the patched open() -- see fopen.c. */
 		fd = open(s, O_RDWR|O_CREAT|O_EXCL, 0600);
 		if (fd >= 0) {
-#ifdef SYS_unlink
-			__syscall(SYS_unlink, s);
-#else
-			__syscall(SYS_unlinkat, AT_FDCWD, s, 0);
-#endif
+			/* pouch: the PUBLIC unlink() (0027's route), errno kept. The
+			 * raw SYS_unlinkat upstream issues here is the 0xFFFF sentinel
+			 * and its result was ignored, so tmpfile() never unlinked: every
+			 * call left a named /tmp/tmpfile_XXXXXX on the persistent root. */
+			int e = errno;
+			unlink(s);
+			errno = e;
 			f = __fdopen(fd, "w+");
 			if (!f) __syscall(SYS_close, fd);
 			return f;
